---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import OfferLadder from '../components/OfferLadder.astro';
import Services from '../components/Services.astro';
import CaseStudies from '../components/CaseStudies.astro';
import DigitalLaunch from '../components/DigitalLaunch.astro';
import HowIWork from '../components/HowIWork.astro';
import CommercialConsultingBlock from '../components/CommercialConsultingBlock.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

{/*
  Retitled 2026-07-29 (4ed2711). This page had been optimized for "AI Consultant
  Oakville", which has no reportable search volume in Canada — it earned 16
  impressions and 0 clicks in 90 days and did not appear in the top 29 for its
  own target term. See docs/keyword-strategy.md.

  On 2026-07-31 (4bb4d18) that fix was reverted and the H1 was narrowed further,
  to "AI Consulting in Oakville for E-Commerce and Product Launch Systems".
  That named two verticals in the most load-bearing line on the money page and
  disqualified most of the actual client roster — a pottery studio, an F45 gym,
  an auto repair shop, a specialty food retailer, a pharma consultancy. Exactly
  one of
  those is e-commerce.

  Reverted again 2026-08-01, deliberately and for the last time:

    - The promise is now problem-based, not industry-based. No vertical appears
      in the H1. The vertical LIST appears lower down, as proof of range.
    - Oakville stays in the NAP and LocalBusiness schema for local trust. It
      does not drive the title. It has no search volume. This is settled.
    - The page leads with the offer ladder (OfferLadder.astro), not the service
      menu. Search Console: /services earned 16 impressions and 0 clicks in 90
      days, and 68% of all site clicks are people searching Greg's name. This
      page's real job is converting warm traffic — meetup attendees, referrals,
      podcast listeners — not capturing cold search. Structure it for the person
      who already knows who Greg is and is deciding whether to book.

  If you are about to put a vertical back in the H1, read docs/positioning.md
  first. The documented primary angle is "The Anti-Consultant", which is
  industry-agnostic by design.
*/}
<Layout
  title="Custom AI Tools & Automation for Small Business | Greg Kowalczyk"
  description="I find the manual work eating your week and build the system that kills it. Custom AI tools you own outright — for any business, not just e-commerce. Free 15-minute assessment. Based in Oakville, working across the GTA."
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <PageHero
      title="I find the manual work eating your week — and I build the system that kills it."
      subtitle="22 years an engineer. 12 running my own brands. Now I build custom AI tools for businesses that need execution, not another strategy deck — pottery studios, auto shops, gyms, specialty food retailers, e-commerce operators. I code it, deploy it, and train your team to run it without me."
    />
    <OfferLadder />
    <CommercialConsultingBlock />
    <Services />
    <CaseStudies />
    <DigitalLaunch />
    <HowIWork />
    <ContactCTA
      heading="Start with 15 free minutes"
      body="Tell me the part of your week that shouldn't need a human. I'll tell you whether AI can take it, name the tool, and give you the first step — at no cost, whether or not we ever work together."
    />
  </main>
  <Footer />
  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll('.fade-in-up').forEach((el) => {
      const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
        (entries) => {
          entries.forEach((entry) => {
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
              entry.target.classList.add('visible');
              observer.unobserve(entry.target);
            }
          });
        },
        { threshold: 0.1 }
      );
      observer.observe(el);
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
